-- INDEPENDENT TESTS (BACKLOG IL-56, tester fid-il-32). Every expected value comes from DECIDED-ANSWERS.md
-- (sha256 dee0c2c8061f14382566aa8ddd7d35c80dc3fc9994899f8c9ca5e786e9b8e726), written from the Hebrew source
-- before this encoding was opened. No expected value was changed to match the encoding.
-- "Case N" is the case number in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md.
--
-- EXPECTED REFUSALS (declared in check.sh as 5 for this module). Each is a #ASSERT of a value I decided, where the encoding refuses:
--   line 123  case 1:  `the full monthly minimum wage ... on` 1 April 1987 = 525 (s 21(a)(1)); the dated entry point refuses before 1 April 2025 (the constant itself is asserted on the next line and passes)
--   line 128  case 3:  30 September 1987 = 525, same
--   line 130  case 4:  1 October 1987 = 551 (s 21(a)(2)), same
--   line 135  case 6:  1 April 2023 = 5,571.75 (the Law's own note, line 23), same
--   line 196  case 45: a zero fraction of a position gives 0; the encoding refuses a zero fraction
-- Cases 68, 69, 70 are tested both ways: the reading I decided is asserted as a value, the default switch as #ASSERT REFUSED.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee`
`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` `the age` MEANS
    `An employee` WITH
        `age in completed years` IS `the age`
        `how pay is fixed` IS `paid by the month`
        `the working week` IS `a six-day working week`
        `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `An employee`
`an independent daily-paid adult, six-day week` MEANS
    `An employee` WITH
        `age in completed years` IS 30
        `how pay is fixed` IS `paid by the day`
        `the working week` IS `a six-day working week`
        `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `An employee`
`an independent daily-paid adult, five-day week` MEANS
    `An employee` WITH
        `age in completed years` IS 30
        `how pay is fixed` IS `paid by the day`
        `the working week` IS `a five-day working week`
        `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `An employee`
`an independent hourly-paid adult` MEANS
    `An employee` WITH
        `age in completed years` IS 30
        `how pay is fixed` IS `paid by the hour`
        `the working week` IS `a five-day working week`
        `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `An employee`
`an independent adult in a section 17 class` MEANS
    `An employee` WITH
        `age in completed years` IS 30
        `how pay is fixed` IS `paid by the month`
        `the working week` IS `a six-day working week`
        `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate` IS TRUE

GIVEN `the hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the full position` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Hours of work in a month`
`independent hours` `the hours` `against` `the full position` MEANS
    `Hours of work in a month` WITH
        `hours the employee works in the month` IS `the hours`
        `hours of a full position customary at the workplace in the month` IS `the full position`

-- A pay of a basic wage, a (zero) cost-of-living supplement and one more component of a given kind and amount.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of pay component`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay for a regular working day`
`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `the kind` `of` `the amount` MEANS
    `Pay for a regular working day` OF
        (LIST
            (`A pay component` OF `a basic wage or a combined wage`, 5_000),
            (`A pay component` OF `a cost-of-living supplement not included in a combined wage`, 0),
            (`A pay component` OF `the kind`, `the amount`)),
        (JUST 5_000)

GIVEN `the basic` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay for a regular working day`
`a pay of a basic wage only` `the basic` MEANS
    `Pay for a regular working day` OF
        (LIST (`A pay component` OF `a basic wage or a combined wage`, `the basic`)),
        (JUST `the basic`)

GIVETH A `Pay for a regular working day`
`a pay of case 67` MEANS
    `Pay for a regular working day` OF
        (LIST
            (`A pay component` OF `a basic wage or a combined wage`, 5_000),
            (`A pay component` OF `a cost-of-living supplement not included in a combined wage`, 500),
            (`A pay component` OF `a fixed supplement paid by reason of the work`, 600),
            (`A pay component` OF `a seniority supplement`, 400),
            (`A pay component` OF `a thirteenth salary`, 300),
            (`A pay component` OF `a refund of expenses, including board, per diem and travel`, 300)),
        (JUST 5_000)

GIVETH A `Pay for a regular working day`
`a pay of case 68` MEANS
    `Pay for a regular working day` OF
        (LIST
            (`A pay component` OF `a basic wage or a combined wage`, 5_000),
            (`A pay component` OF `a fixed supplement paid by reason of the work`, 600)),
        (JUST 5_000)

GIVETH A `Pay for a regular working day`
`a pay of case 71, commission only` MEANS
    `Pay for a regular working day` OF
        (LIST (`A pay component` OF `a component the text does not name`, 7_000)),
        (JUST 7_000)

§ `Part A: the monthly minimum`

-- Case 1: 1 April 1987 = 525 (s 21(a)(1)). The constant exists; the dated entry point is asked.
#ASSERT `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 1987 4 1) EQUALS 525
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage that section 21(a)(1) fixes for 1 April 1987` EQUALS 525
-- Case 2: 31 March 1987, law not in force (s 20): a refusal is the right outcome (the reason differs, see findings).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 1987 3 31) BECAUSE "no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025"
-- Case 3: 30 September 1987 = 525.
#ASSERT `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 1987 9 30) EQUALS 525
-- Case 4: 1 October 1987 = 551 (s 21(a)(2)).
#ASSERT `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 1987 10 1) EQUALS 551
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage that section 21(a)(2) fixes for 1 October 1987` EQUALS 551
-- Case 5: 1990 has no figure in the sources: refusal expected.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 1990 1 1) BECAUSE "no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025"
-- Case 6: 1 April 2023 = 5,571.75 (the Law's note on line 23).
#ASSERT `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 2023 4 1) EQUALS 5_571.75
-- Case 7: AW 13,566 -> 6,443.85 ; case 9: AW 12,000 -> 5,700 ; AW 11,730 -> 5,571.75.
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage on 1 April, before increases under section 4, from` 13_566 EQUALS 6_443.85
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage on 1 April, before increases under section 4, from` 12_000 EQUALS 5_700
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage on 1 April, before increases under section 4, from` 11_730 EQUALS 5_571.75
-- Case 10: s 5, AW falls: previous 6,443.85, computed 0.475 x 13,000 = 6,175 -> 6,443.85.
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage after an update, given` 6_443.85 `and` (`the monthly minimum wage on 1 April, before increases under section 4, from` 13_000) EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 11: previous 5,571.75, computed 6,443.85 -> 6,443.85.
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage after an update, given` 5_571.75 `and` (`the monthly minimum wage on 1 April, before increases under section 4, from` 13_566) EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 12: equal -> unchanged.
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage after an update, given` 6_443.85 `and` 6_443.85 EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 8: 2026-04-01 onwards is covered by the published figure.
#ASSERT `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 6_443.85

§ `Part B: daily and hourly`

-- Cases 17-24, daily; exact: daily x 65 = M x 3 (five-day), daily x 25 = M (six-day).
#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage from` 5_571.75 `for` `a six-day working week` EQUALS 222.87
#ASSERT (`the daily minimum wage from` 5_571.75 `for` `a five-day working week`) TIMES 65 EQUALS 16_715.25
#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage from` 6_443.85 `for` `a six-day working week` EQUALS 257.754
#ASSERT (`the daily minimum wage from` 6_443.85 `for` `a five-day working week`) TIMES 65 EQUALS 19_331.55
#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage from` 525 `for` `a six-day working week` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT (`the daily minimum wage from` 525 `for` `a five-day working week`) TIMES 65 EQUALS 1_575
#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage from` 551 `for` `a six-day working week` EQUALS 22.04
#ASSERT (`the daily minimum wage from` 551 `for` `a five-day working week`) TIMES 65 EQUALS 1_653
-- Case 31: five-day daily exceeds six-day daily.
#ASSERT (`the daily minimum wage from` 6_443.85 `for` `a five-day working week`) GREATER THAN (`the daily minimum wage from` 6_443.85 `for` `a six-day working week`)
-- Cases 26-29, hourly (divisor 186 from the deposited text; 182 flagged as source-currency risk A4).
#ASSERT (`the hourly minimum wage from` 5_571.75) TIMES 186 EQUALS 5_571.75
#ASSERT (`the hourly minimum wage from` 6_443.85) TIMES 186 EQUALS 6_443.85
#ASSERT (`the hourly minimum wage from` 525) TIMES 186 EQUALS 525
#ASSERT (`the hourly minimum wage from` 551) TIMES 186 EQUALS 551
-- Case 30: the divisor is fixed.
#ASSERT `the hours in a month that the hourly minimum wage assumes` EQUALS 186

§ `Part C: coverage`

-- Case 32/35: adults. Case 34: 18 exactly.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 18) `from` 6_443.85 EQUALS 6_443.85
#ASSERT `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 40) `from` 6_443.85 EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 33, 36: under 18 -> s 16 regulations.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 17) `from` 6_443.85 BECAUSE "the rate for an employee under 18 is fixed by regulations under section 16, which this model does not hold; the Law itself prints none"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 15) `from` 6_443.85 BECAUSE "the rate for an employee under 18 is fixed by regulations under section 16, which this model does not hold; the Law itself prints none"
-- Cases 37, 38: s 17 classes.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `an independent adult in a section 17 class` `from` 6_443.85 BECAUSE "the rate for an employee in a class that section 17 regulations may cover is fixed by regulations this model does not hold"
-- As the case may be: daily, hourly bases.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `an independent daily-paid adult, six-day week` `from` 6_443.85 EQUALS 257.754
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `an independent daily-paid adult, five-day week` `from` 6_443.85) TIMES 65 EQUALS 19_331.55
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `an independent hourly-paid adult` `from` 6_443.85) TIMES 186 EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Cases 39-41: pay against the minimum 6,443.85.
#ASSERT `the pay meets the minimum wage:` (`a pay of a basic wage only` 6_443.85) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` `against` 6_443.85 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the pay meets the minimum wage:` (`a pay of a basic wage only` 6_443.84) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` `against` 6_443.85 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the pay meets the minimum wage:` (`a pay of a basic wage only` 7_000) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` `against` 6_443.85 EQUALS TRUE
-- Case 42: half a position.
#ASSERT `the partial minimum wage under section 2(b) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 30) `from` 6_443.85 `at the fraction` 0.5 EQUALS 3_221.925
-- Case 43: 30 of 42 hours, reading A named; the default declines because 42 is not 186.
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage of a part-time position under section 2(b) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 30) `from` 6_443.85 `on` (`independent hours` 30 `against` (JUST 42)) `read` `by the hours of a full position customary at the workplace`) TIMES 42 EQUALS 193_315.5
#ASSERT REFUSED `the minimum wage of a part-time position under section 2(b) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 30) `from` 6_443.85 `on` (`independent hours` 30 `against` (JUST 42)) `read` `decline where the readings differ` BECAUSE "the Law does not decide how to measure the fraction of a part-time position by hours: reading A uses the hours of a full position customary at the workplace, reading B the 186 hours of s 1, and they give different answers here"
-- Case 44: full.
#ASSERT `the partial minimum wage under section 2(b) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 30) `from` 6_443.85 `at the fraction` 1 EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 45: 0% of a position -> 0. The encoding refuses a zero fraction.
#ASSERT `the partial minimum wage under section 2(b) for` (`an independent monthly-paid employee aged` 30) `from` 6_443.85 `at the fraction` 0 EQUALS 0

§ `Part D: absence`

-- Case 49: none.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage after an absence, from` 6_443.85 `with absence of` 0 `and arrangement payment` NOTHING EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 50: whole month, unpaid.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage after an absence, from` 6_443.85 `with absence of` 1 `and arrangement payment` NOTHING EQUALS 0
-- Case 51: half.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage after an absence, from` 6_443.85 `with absence of` 0.5 `and arrangement payment` NOTHING EQUALS 3_221.925
-- Case 52: 2 of 22 working days: 6,443.85 x 20 / 22 ; x 22 = 128,877.
#ASSERT (`the minimum wage after an absence, from` 6_443.85 `with absence of` (2 DIVIDED BY 22) `and arrangement payment` NOTHING) TIMES 22 EQUALS 128_877
-- Cases 53/54: quarter absent, arrangement pays 900 for that time: 6,443.85 x 0.75 + 900 = 5,732.8875.
#ASSERT `the minimum wage after an absence, from` 6_443.85 `with absence of` 0.25 `and arrangement payment` (JUST 900) EQUALS 5_732.8875

§ `Part E: which pay counts (s 3)`

-- Cases 55-56: a basic wage counts in full.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of a basic wage only` 6_443.85) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 6_443.85
-- Case 59: a fixed supplement counts (basic 5,000 + 0 + 600).
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a fixed supplement paid by reason of the work` `of` 600) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_600
-- Cases 60-66: each excluded kind adds nothing (100 each).
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a family supplement` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a seniority supplement` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a supplement for shift work` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a measured, agreed, fixed or group premium` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a thirteenth salary` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `an annual grant` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a refund of expenses, including board, per diem and travel` `of` 100) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_000
-- Case 57: a separate cost-of-living supplement counts.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a cost-of-living supplement not included in a combined wage` `of` 500) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_500
-- Case 67: 5,000 + 500 + 600 = 6,100; shortfall 343.85 against 6,443.85.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` `a pay of case 67` `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 6_100
#ASSERT `the pay meets the minimum wage:` `a pay of case 67` `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` `against` 6_443.85 EQUALS FALSE
-- Case 68: combined wage + fixed supplement: I decided 5,600 (reading P); the default declines.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` `a pay of case 68` `read` `only when the pay has neither a basic or combined wage nor a cost-of-living supplement` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 5_600
#ASSERT REFUSED `the pay that counts for` `a pay of case 68` `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` BECAUSE "sections 3(b) and 3(d) do not decide which pay counts here: the allowed readings (whether section 3(d) applies, whether an unlisted component counts) give different amounts"
-- Cases 69/70: overtime and employer pension contributions (unnamed): I decided they do not count.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a component the text does not name` `of` 800) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `it does not count` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the pay that counts for` (`a pay of basic 5000, COLA 0 and one extra` `a component the text does not name` `of` 800) `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` BECAUSE "sections 3(b) and 3(d) do not decide which pay counts here: the allowed readings (whether section 3(d) applies, whether an unlisted component counts) give different amounts"
-- Case 71: commission only, regular pay 7,000 -> 3(d) applies on both readings.
#ASSERT `the pay that counts for` `a pay of case 71, commission only` `read` `decline where the readings differ` `and` `decline where the readings differ` EQUALS 7_000

§ `Part F: delegation, outside the encoding`

-- Case 8b: no AW supplied for 1 April 2027: refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` (YMD 2027 4 1) BECAUSE "the full monthly minimum wage from 1 April 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched"
-- Cases 73-78 (s 18 regulations, penalties amounts), 13-15 (s 4 increase), 79-83 (ss 6A, 7B): no entry point exists; SCOPE, see findings.
